# Architecture: Application Layer

- The application layer must orchestrate business workflows and contain use cases.
- Module application code must live under `app/modules/<module>/application`.
- Use cases must live under `app/modules/<module>/application/use_cases`.
- Application DTOs must live in `app/modules/<module>/application/dto.py`.
- Each use case must represent one business scenario and define the operation order for that scenario.
- Application code may coordinate repositories, domain services, technical services, and application services through contracts.
- Application code must control transaction boundaries. Multiple repository operations in one workflow must commit together and roll back together on failure.
- Application code must depend only on interfaces and contracts, not concrete infrastructure implementations.
- Do not import FastAPI routers, HTTP request objects, HTTP response objects, or route-specific Pydantic schemas into application code.
- Do not write raw SQLAlchemy queries in application code. Persistence access belongs behind repository contracts.
- Do not localize messages in business workflow logic. Raise stable error codes and let API boundary handlers localize responses.
